bevy-horizon: count compute invocations in statistics queries that count graphics work too

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 606441c9, after 0001-0016. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this text before the first
"diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

Mesa's a10c12e6 ("nvk: Only increment CS counters when query is active in CmdDispatchBase", by
Mary Guillemard, mesa/mesa!42732), which mesa-switch carries, made a direct dispatch add its
compute invocations only while cmd->state.cs.active_compute_invocations_query is set. Two cases
leave it clear while a query that counts them is active:

- A pipeline-statistics pool that counts compute invocations and any graphics statistic.
  nvk_cmd_set_statistics_counters sets the flag only in the else of
  "statistics_counter_mask != 0", and compute invocations have no bit in that mask, so such a
  pool reads 0 compute invocations for every direct dispatch, on every GPU NVK supports. Bevy's
  RenderDiagnosticsPlugin times each pass with one such pool, every statistic in it
  (bevy_render 0.18.1, diagnostic/internal.rs). Skate 3's per-pass figures drop zeros, so its
  direct dispatches' compute invocations went missing from them without a sign.
- vkCmdExecuteCommands clears cmd->state.cs, the flag with it, so the primary's dispatches after
  it stop counting while the query is still active. wgpu records no secondary command buffers,
  so Bevy doesn't reach this one.

The flag is now set whatever else the pool counts, and vkCmdExecuteCommands keeps it. Indirect
dispatches add their invocations in a macro without checking the flag, so they were never
affected. Mesa's main branch had the same code on 11 October 2026.

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c
index 60ae745..85cb5bc 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -699,8 +699,15 @@ nvk_CmdExecuteCommands(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
     * dirty tracking, we may miss the fact that a secondary has messed with
     * GPU state if we don't invalidate all our internal tracking.
    */
+   /* A query begun in the primary is still active after the secondaries, so
+    * its dispatches must keep adding compute invocations.
+    */
+   const bool active_compute_invocations_query =
+      cmd->state.cs.active_compute_invocations_query;
    nvk_cmd_invalidate_graphics_state(cmd);
    nvk_cmd_invalidate_compute_state(cmd);
+   cmd->state.cs.active_compute_invocations_query =
+      active_compute_invocations_query;
 }
 
 enum nvk_barrier {
diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_query_pool.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_query_pool.c
index ceda24f..74d8c58 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_query_pool.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_query_pool.c
@@ -670,9 +670,13 @@ nvk_cmd_set_statistics_counters(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd,
          P_1INC(p, NV9097, CALL_MME_MACRO(NVK_MME_SET_STATISTICS_COUNTERS));
          P_INLINE_DATA(p, enable);
          P_INLINE_DATA(p, pool->statistics_counter_mask);
-      } else if (pool->vk.query_type == VK_QUERY_TYPE_PIPELINE_STATISTICS &&
-                 pool->vk.pipeline_statistics &
-                    VK_QUERY_PIPELINE_STATISTIC_COMPUTE_SHADER_INVOCATIONS_BIT) {
+      }
+      /* Compute invocations have no bit in statistics_counter_mask, so this
+       * is set whatever graphics statistics the pool also counts.
+       */
+      if (pool->vk.query_type == VK_QUERY_TYPE_PIPELINE_STATISTICS &&
+          pool->vk.pipeline_statistics &
+             VK_QUERY_PIPELINE_STATISTIC_COMPUTE_SHADER_INVOCATIONS_BIT) {
          cmd->state.cs.active_compute_invocations_query = enable;
       }
       break;
